the spring semester at the University of  Idaho starts today that's nearly two  months after four students were murdered  in their house near the campus 28 year  old Brian coburger was arrested late  last month and charged with the killings  Lilia Luciano reports on the reaction  from the campus in Moscow Idaho  it was a shock for many of our our  students that something like this would  happen here the spring semester is  underway at the University of Idaho dean  of students Blaine eichel said the goal  of the administration is to return a  sense of normalcy for students our  students want to be in community they  want to be here for many students it'll  be the first time back on campus since  the murders of Kaylee Gonzalez Madison  Mogan zaneker nodal and Ethan Chapin  eichel says safety is a top priority  we've increased the relationship with  the Lata County Sheriff's Office so  they're going to have a presence on  campus we've also hired additional  campus security officers and we're still  in very close partnership with the  Moscow Police Department Stu students  were on winter break when Brian coburger  was arrested on December 30th for the  murders which happened at the women's  off-campus home in the early morning  hours of November 13th we sat down with  five freshmen at the University some of  them expressed praise for law  enforcement and a sense of relief that a  suspect was in custody including 18 year  olds Aiden hedinger and Cole pawlik what  they did and what in relatively a short  amount of time inclined it was kind of a  relief just knowing that they have  someone but others like Madeline Pollock  also a teen are still on edge  I'm very paranoid so I kept a lot of my  safety still up 18 year old twins Owen  and Olivia West say the crime  transformed campus life I had never like  originally walked with like a knife for  like my keys between my fingers before  fearing for their safety the twins did  not return to campus after Thanksgiving  break and are still grappling with one  question why them some of them are just  starting like their new life like why  did you take that from them  as much as Campus Life is starting to  get back to normal here at the  University this case is only now getting  started Brian coburger the suspect is  expected back in court tomorrow morning  and if he is convicted he faces the  death penalty and Nate I'm already  hearing a lot of support for that here  in town  Lilia thank you
 

